---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
	title="About | BlogToolStack"
	description="Why BlogToolStack exists and how we pick the email marketing and creator tools we cover."
>
	<div class="content-page">
		<h1>About BlogToolStack</h1>
		<p>
			BlogToolStack helps bloggers and creators choose the right email marketing tools without
			wading through marketing copy. Every comparison, review, and guide here comes from actually
			using the tools, not just reading their feature pages.
		</p>
		<p>
			The site is run by <strong>Joel</strong>, a Japan-based creator who builds and tests
			email marketing and creator-economy tools as part of a broader interest in automation
			and content systems.
		</p>

		<h2>How we pick what to cover</h2>
		<p>
			We start from the questions bloggers actually ask when they're choosing an email tool for
			the first time, or deciding whether to switch: what it costs as a list grows, what's
			locked behind a paid plan, and where it falls short compared to alternatives. Articles are
			written to be useful on their own, whether or not you ever click an affiliate link.
		</p>

		<h2>How this site makes money</h2>
		<p>
			BlogToolStack earns affiliate commissions when readers sign up for tools like Kit through
			links on this site, at no extra cost to you. This never changes what we say about a
			product's strengths or weaknesses. Every article that includes an affiliate link
			says so clearly. See our <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> for more on how data and
			links on this site work.
		</p>

		<h2>Questions or feedback?</h2>
		<p>
			Reach out any time via the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
		</p>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>
